    "body": "## Summary\n- add owner-only `GET /jobs/publications/pending` for active, unexpired `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` publication attempts\n- keep recovery privacy-safe: responses contain only the existing payment/publication summary and never serialized job payload, exact address, route payload, Stripe secret, or another user's publication\n- sort recoverable attempts newest-first\n- make Create Job automatically resume the newest unfinished publication after reload or reopening the page\n- reuse the existing Payment Element/payment-intent flow, cancellation semantics, webhook settlement and polling instead of creating a second payment path\n- add focused service regression coverage for owner scoping and anonymous enumeration denial\n\n## Why\nPR #92 made publish-with-wallet-plus-Stripe safe and idempotent, but the browser only retained a pending publication ID in component state. Reloading, reopening the page, or moving to another device therefore stranded the UX until the reservation expired. This slice makes the existing server-side state discoverable by its owner and reconnects the frontend to it.\n\n## Privacy / accounting\n- only `PAYMENT_REQUIRED` rows owned by the authenticated user and not past `expiresAt` are discoverable\n- no pending publication becomes a public Job\n- no wallet movement occurs during recovery reads\n- reservation release remains exclusively in existing cancel/expiry/settlement paths\n- no schema or Flyway migration is required\n\nDo not merge until every latest-head CI/check is green.",
